<title>UK: Granada falls on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Granada falls on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in media and leisure company Granada Group fell 12 pence to 770-1/2 as profit-taking ended a short-lived bull run, dealers said.</p>
<p>Granada perked up late last week after closing at a 12-month low of 738 pence on July 10 following a period of prolonged underperformance.</p>
<p>Worries over apparent falls in television advertising revenues depressed the shares in the past three months, but broker Lehman Brothers on Friday said the stocks looked oversold.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
